  BOT@{ shape: cloud, label: "Keeper bot<br/>(merchant-run cron,<br/>replaceable by anyone)" }
  K(["Caller: anyone<br/>signer, pays Charge rent"]):::signer
  BOT --> K
  K -->|"process_billing"| IX["process_billing"]:::billing
  IX --> D1{"subscription.status == Active?"}
  D1 -- no --> E1["Error: SubscriptionNotActive"]:::err
  D1 -- yes --> D2{"now ≥ next_billing_ts?"}
  D2 -- no --> E2["Error: NotDue"]:::err
  D2 -- yes --> D0{"subscriber_ata == canonical USDC ATA of subscription.subscriber?<br/>vault == PDA(vault, subscription)?"}
  D0 -- no --> E0["Error: WrongTokenAccount"]:::err
  D0 -- yes --> D3{"subscriber ATA: delegate == Delegate PDA,<br/>delegated_amount ≥ price,<br/>amount ≥ price, not frozen?"}
  D3 -- "no · REQ-09" --> L1["status = Lapsed · plan.subs_count −= 1<br/>emit SubscriptionLapsed<br/>NO transfer; the tx succeeds"]:::billing
  D3 -- "yes · REQ-08" --> T1["transfer_checked CPI<br/>subscriber ATA → Vault PDA<br/>amount = subscription.price (snapshot)<br/>authority: Delegate PDA (signs with seeds)"]:::billing
  T1 --> C1["init Charge PDA · seeds: charge, subscription, cycle<br/>state = Held, pulled_at = now, rent_payer = caller"]:::pda
  C1 --> U1["cycle += 1 · next_billing_ts += interval_secs<br/>open_charges += 1 · held_total += price<br/>emit ChargePulled"]:::billing
  T1 -.->|"CPI"| SPL["SPL Token program"]:::xprog
  C1 -.->|"CPI"| SYS["System program"]:::xprog
  SATA["Subscriber USDC ATA"]:::tok ==>|"price"| VAULT["Vault PDA · vault, subscription"]:::pda
  SPL -.- SATA

  N1["In the SubStack LOI design a failed pull would revert the whole tx, so Lapsed would be unreachable.<br/>Balance and allowance are now checked before the CPI."]:::note
  N2["The program, not the allowance, limits each subscription to one price per interval."]:::note
  N4["Critical check: the Delegate PDA is the delegate on EVERY subscriber's ATA,<br/>so without pinning the ATA to subscription.subscriber a caller could bill<br/>subscription A from subscriber B's wallet."]:::note
  D0 -.- N4
  N3["Late keeper: one cycle per call, so repeated calls catch up."]:::note
  L1 -.- N1
  T1 -.- N2
  U1 -.- N3
